    "seconds": 113,
    "summary": "Payment has stopped failing: 0 \"Invalid token\" errors and 1 successful charge request in the last 40 seconds.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause:** The `paymentFailure` flag in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `defaultVariant: \"100%\"`, so the payment service failed 100% of charge requests with \"Payment request failed. Invalid token.\" Checkout and the frontend then failed for every user. The upstream demo default is `\"off\"`.\n\n**Fix:** I changed `paymentFailure.defaultVariant` from `\"100%\"` to `\"off\"` in `flagd-config` and ran `kubectl rollout restart deployment/flagd`. The restart was needed because flagd's init container copies the config into an emptyDir, so a ConfigMap edit alone doesn't reach the running pod.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 29 pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running with 0 restarts.\n- Payment logged 0 \"Invalid token\" errors in the last 40 seconds and processed a charge request normally.\n\n**Notes:**\n- The `payment` and `flagd` rollouts I saw at the start were `kubectl rollout restart`s with identical specs. They weren't the cause.\n- The ConfigMap is managed by Helm (`app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: Helm`). A future `helm upgrade` could reset this flag from the chart values, so the flag value should also be fixed in the source values file or the release.\n- I did not confirm the flagd file contents from inside the pod, because the flagd image has no `cat`. I verified the ConfigMap directly and the payment behaviour changed as expected.",
    "timed_out": false,
    "turns": 16,
